<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Iran: Activists sound alarm as regime seizes Baha'i assets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfb23b9f40640c92619edd9ccf3c20aa9c6f9a7a1ff4e57419ca0235dca484e0</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-activists-sound-alarm-as-regime-seizes-baha-i-assets/a-79291138--d67cdfeb619f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-activists-sound-alarm-as-regime-seizes-baha-i-assets/a-79291138?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rights groups warn Iran is increasingly confiscating assets from government critics and members of the country's Baha'i faith, but also actors, athletes, and journalists living abroad.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Poland reaffirms support for Ukraine after drone strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71ee9d06e1ea2c3ee225a528450f1ebbdf7d01a3945b57661b8d0e2d6e71681d</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-reaffirms-support-for-ukraine-after-drone-strikes/a-79291144--da0463d9d7dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-reaffirms-support-for-ukraine-after-drone-strikes/a-79291144?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After Russia's recent drone attacks on targets close to the Ukraine-Poland border, Warsaw has doubled down on its support for Kyiv and pledged a "nonprovocative but serious response" to Moscow.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Belarus to release 25 more prisoners as US eases sanctions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0852106e632b72885bccd719f5f15d93af1f108022bbed70ff49b6c3348fc743</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:35:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T12:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/belarus-to-release-25-more-prisoners-as-us-eases-sanctions/a-79290676--44b5cc402b01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/belarus-to-release-25-more-prisoners-as-us-eases-sanctions/a-79290676?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Belarus will release 25 more prisoners under an interim agreement with the United States, while Washington plans to lift sanctions on two Belarusian companies and pursue broader negotiations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Congo's Ebola epidemic may have gone unnoticed for months</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1812ba865db49b30499724790aabb9608c96260e0471df8f52af0e59e2b88df3</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T11:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-epidemic-may-have-gone-unnoticed-for-months/a-79281803--5e7710f3265e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-epidemic-may-have-gone-unnoticed-for-months/a-79281803?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The deadliest Ebola outbreak on record in the Democratic Republic of Congo may have begun months before it was first declared in May.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: US bill sanctioning Russia could hit India with tariffs of up to 100%</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50d9cd92717e75adb2ac4f32440b37d0cbbd2be043ca6a2075ed13b9d62cdfa1</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T11:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-us-bill-sanctioning-russia-could-hit-india-with-tariffs-of-up-to-100/live-79285577--613ee224f2db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-us-bill-sanctioning-russia-could-hit-india-with-tariffs-of-up-to-100/live-79285577?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new bill could give President Trump the power to impose tariffs of up to 100% on countries buying Russian oil and gas, potentially affecting major importer India.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Conservative state premiers rally behind Merz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:145eff4890d8b2dc92e0dee40ec8efd5702fe98035c29fb2f57967151f80b743</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T11:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-conservative-state-premiers-rally-behind-merz/live-79289786--e3b9d59d079d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-conservative-state-premiers-rally-behind-merz/live-79289786?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">All eight CDU state premiers have backed Friedrich Merz, urging the party to focus on rebuilding trust. Plus, Germany's coalition is weighing rapid relief as record fuel prices pile pressure on households. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Duterte makes first appearance before ICC judges</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6e0dfe4f96301e8d194780fa479c4d6f9ef5ddaf1c661a365de482244530a9d</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/duterte-makes-first-appearance-before-icc-judges/a-79288207--0d857df202d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/duterte-makes-first-appearance-before-icc-judges/a-79288207?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former Philippine President Rodrigo Duterte appeared in person at the ICC as judges considered claims of memory impairment and poor health. The 81-year-old is accused of crimes against humanity.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Chancellor Merz fighting for political survival</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43e7b2d4c47856c250923d6de3c6f21b07ce93c6f07a556d0952dd2ef218a214</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T10:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-chancellor-merz-fighting-for-political-survival/a-79290192--4c7403d99c36.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-chancellor-merz-fighting-for-political-survival/a-79290192?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following the CDU's crushing defeat in the Saxony-Anhalt state election, many are expressing doubts about their party leader, Chancellor Friedrich Merz. But they don't appear to have any viable alternative.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>US charges 5 people over Russia-backed plots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:477964e0f4507ba061559807c3de89b53de090f4ce82044a2d9a07183f3093d3</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T10:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-charges-5-people-over-russia-backed-plots/a-79285863--41f6aef6be3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-charges-5-people-over-russia-backed-plots/a-79285863?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US prosecutors accuse the foreign nationals of conducting surveillance, attacks, and murder-for-hire operations for Moscow — just after a DW investigation identified one of the suspects as a salsa teacher in Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US announces South Africa visa curbs over race claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09068876616509182ab82b3806269cd854fffad7482632c4d7a33ea0c27bb7a4</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-announces-south-africa-visa-curbs-over-race-claims/a-79288287--ba8545978a2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-announces-south-africa-visa-curbs-over-race-claims/a-79288287?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The visa restriction policy targets South African nationals who US Secretary of State Marco Rubio claims are responsible for "race-based discrimination" against white citizens.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Global Gender Gap Report: Women's hard-won gains 'fragile'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ba3625f8204882bdf5c2f7cd6ca6853a3163f94bf41a8f4d62de06a1646ab0a</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T10:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-gender-gap-report-women-s-hard-won-gains-fragile/a-79280086--9ed95bd98a77.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-gender-gap-report-women-s-hard-won-gains-fragile/a-79280086?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two decades of progress toward gender parity is at risk as women's political representation declines, according to a new World Economic Forum report. At the current pace, the remaining gap could take 120 years to close.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Kosovo ex-president Thaci sentenced to 25 years for war crimes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d5524b3a19e5b77256f8090aace9f4f1eebd46d1d61a61c1917756e85d683f6</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kosovo-ex-president-thaci-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes/a-79286344--737389b3e2ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kosovo-ex-president-thaci-sentenced-to-25-years-for-war-crimes/a-79286344?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Hague tribunal ruled that Hashim Thaci, a former leader of the Kosovo Liberation Army (KLA), is responsible for war crimes carried out during the war of independence with Serbia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German drama 'Blindspot Berlin' revisits 2016 Christmas market attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d40af5cffaeba216abf585ff1a1633964f71f0c887d505d5fc2e42222f9e211f</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-drama-blindspot-berlin-revisits-2016-christmas-market-attack/a-79281162--11e3e3b69ad1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-drama-blindspot-berlin-revisits-2016-christmas-market-attack/a-79281162?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A decade after the terrorist attack on a Berlin Christmas market, a new German miniseries looks into the institutional failures that allowed the deadly truck rampage to happen.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Von der Leyen eyes Canada as EU's first 'associate member'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0f5892b1d5d0c6d857e50ff2775f3ef6fc75940ccb5626c2793c3d626d880db</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/von-der-leyen-eyes-canada-as-eu-s-first-associate-member/a-79286148--80704c7f35c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/von-der-leyen-eyes-canada-as-eu-s-first-associate-member/a-79286148?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU chief Ursula von der Leyen said the EU and Canada saw the world with the same eyes. At her annual State of the Union address, she said the bloc was dealing with an "openly hostile world."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia says Houthis target Mecca, warns of 'red line'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26f50a04794ea66266026b65916c154c086afaa96832c30cf0e12418a31fcac3</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-says-houthis-target-mecca-warns-of-red-line/a-79285099--daeebd4869ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-says-houthis-target-mecca-warns-of-red-line/a-79285099?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Saudi-led coalition said its air defenses had destroyed a Houthi-deployed drone just outside Mecca, Islam's holiest city.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How hotter weather is making us poorer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b19acce72694ecc49a7056c3cea957c3cfeccd16b5c44eead954fa251f82c70</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T08:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-hotter-weather-is-making-us-poorer/a-79268306--10853d8a0a0a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-hotter-weather-is-making-us-poorer/a-79268306?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Heat waves, wildfires and floods have cascading economic impacts, causing incomes to decline and the price of basic goods to rise. The trend will escalate as temperatures continue to increase.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>News helicopter crashes in LA, killing 3</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f51d9e617c336c4d2c9ca296d68569b9339039a9252f314831444147e96a060d</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T05:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/news-helicopter-crashes-in-la-killing-3/a-79285216--a9e0baeb110d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/news-helicopter-crashes-in-la-killing-3/a-79285216?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A helicopter belonging to an NBC news affiliate was covering a large traffic accident in the southern California city when it crashed. The cause is currently unclear.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Supporting acts pull out of Ed Sheeran's tour over dropping Macklemore</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d3a85524ade581786fe2915ee4b3a6b7f36d01920e7860fceb80c222b98af65</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:34:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T00:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/supporting-acts-pull-out-of-ed-sheeran-s-tour-over-dropping-macklemore/a-79284880--110e4c18341a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/supporting-acts-pull-out-of-ed-sheeran-s-tour-over-dropping-macklemore/a-79284880?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Macklemore was dropped over his pro-Palestinian stance, amid accusations of antisemitism. Sheeran said removing the artist was not his decision but that of the tour's promoters.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>AI leaders call for regulations, Trump dismisses 'hoaxes'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ce5388dc13f9b39122b942d4f994f1d7761e1590cc09911b98016b19e65f850</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:34:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T22:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-leaders-call-for-regulations-trump-dismisses-hoaxes/a-79284638--467266d159bd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-leaders-call-for-regulations-trump-dismisses-hoaxes/a-79284638?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI giants are working to create a standards body amid rising alarms about the dangers of the industry. Meanwhile, Trump has dismissed the warnings, and a divided US Congress has failed to act.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey's rights groups, EU call out LGBTQ+ crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3257ce9b1b261044f449e725b0fee101cad0cc0e4e35a247bacc75c23f15360b</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T19:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-rights-groups-eu-call-out-lgbtq-crackdown/a-79284021--701b89ffacea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-rights-groups-eu-call-out-lgbtq-crackdown/a-79284021?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several raids and arrests of LGBTQ+ persons in Turkey have triggered sharp criticism from numerous Turkish organizations — and also from Brussels.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Drivers in Germany fume over soaring fuel prices</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:232b31482b5802799128337c6cd5590f93bf05fb287f530cf5d902449e0dd837</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T16:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/drivers-in-germany-fume-over-soaring-fuel-prices/a-79282456--6a933389e322.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/drivers-in-germany-fume-over-soaring-fuel-prices/a-79282456?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz wants to provide relief to motorists. But exactly how this is to happen remains unclear.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry></feed>
